-- title:
--   Surjectivity of Ihara's amalgam map onto Γ₀ away from q
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ and $q$ be natural numbers with $N$ and $q$ coprime and $q$ prime. Consider the group `iharaAmalgam N q`, defined as the pushout `Monoid.PushoutI (iharaEdge N q)` of the edge datum `iharaEdge N q` (the amalgam of two vertex groups along one edge group), and the subgroup `Gamma0Away N q` of $\mathrm{SL}(2, \mathtt{ZAway } q)$ consisting of those matrices $g$ for which the image of $N$ in the ring `ZAway q` divides the lower-left entry $g_{1,0}$. The homomorphism [`Ihara.amalgamToGamma0Away N q`](def/IharaAmalgamMap.html#L141) is the restriction to this subgroup of the homomorphism [`Ihara.amalgamToAway N q`](def/IharaAmalgamMap.html#L87) obtained, via `iharaLift`, from the two vertex homomorphisms `vertexZero N q` and `vertexOne N q` into $\mathrm{SL}(2, \mathtt{ZAway } q)$ together with their agreement `vertex_compat N q` on the edge group; its image lands in `Gamma0Away N q` by `amalgamToAway_mem N q`. The assertion is that this homomorphism from the amalgam to `Gamma0Away N q` is surjective as a function.
--
--   This is the surjectivity half of Ihara's amalgam decomposition: the subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2$ over $\mathbb{Z}$ with $q$ inverted given by the congruence condition modulo $N$ on the lower-left entry is generated by its two vertex subgroups, so that together with injectivity it identifies the group with the amalgam $\Gamma_0(N) *_{\Gamma_0(Nq)} \Gamma_0(N)$. It is used downstream in the study of the abelianisation of `Gamma0Away N q`, in the construction of elements acting trivially on prescribed data, and in an invariance statement for cusp forms under the Hecke diagonal matrix.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Ihara_amalgamToGamma0Away_surjective.lean

